<title>UK: EMI gains amid positive NatWest comments.</title>
<headline>EMI gains amid positive NatWest comments.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in EMI Group Plc advanced on Wednesday after the stock was tipped as a good long term play by analysts at NatWest Securities.</p>
<p>The shares were up 26p at 11.70 stg by 0854 GMT.</p>
<p>Market sources said NatWest highlighted the shares along with other sector favourites, Pearson Plc and United News &amp; Media Plc.  </p>
<p>Shares in Pearson were up 2-1/2p at 746p and United News also gained 2-1/2p to 745-1/2p. Both were said to offer long-term potential amid restructuring hopes.</p>
<p>Analysts at NatWest downgraded the media sector last December from overweight to neutral, they maintain a neutral stance following the sector's five percent underperformance in the last four months.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
